<title>UK: Dawn Til Dusk sets premium on AIM debut.</title>
<headline>Dawn Til Dusk sets premium on AIM debut.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in retailer Dawn Til Dusk Plc set a premium on their first day of trade on the London Stock Exchange's Alternative Investment Market (AIM) on Friday.</p>
<p>The shares were quoted at 121-1/2p by 1225 GMT, setting a premium to the 115p issue price, although no trade was registered in the stock.</p>
<p>The float valued the convenience store operator and discount liquor retailer, which is based in the North West of England, at 4.04 million stg and raised 1.5 million stg.</p>
<p>Butterfield Securities was broker and adviser to the issue.</p>
<p>-- John Sutherland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7945</p>
